# This file exists specifically to keep real secrets out of Docker build
# contexts in this repo — most importantly apps/dash/.env, which on g510
# holds a live GitHub App private key (Contents/Actions/Pull-requests write
# on AdingApkgg/adx-dl) plus the Cloudflare Access AUD tag. Without this
# file, `docker compose up -d --build` (context: repo root, per
# apps/dash/compose.yaml) would tar that file into the build context and
# apps/dash/Dockerfile's builder stage would COPY it into an image layer —
# recoverable later via `docker history` / `docker save` / the build cache,
# even though the final runner stage never copies it forward. Do not delete
# this file without replacing what it does. apps/dash/Dockerfile also lists
# its builder-stage COPY sources explicitly (not a directory-wide copy) as
# a second, independent line of defense — the two are meant to overlap.
#
# Secondary purpose: apps/dash's Dockerfile only ever needs a handful of
# package.json manifests plus apps/dash's own source — everything else
# below is either generated output, VCS/tooling metadata, or unrelated
# workspace content (large data/asset directories included) that would
# otherwise be tarred up and sent to the Docker daemon on every build.

# --- secrets: exclude every .env variant at any depth, keep the template ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# --- VCS / editor metadata: never needed inside a build ---
.git
**/.gitignore
**/.DS_Store

# --- generated output: the builder stage produces these itself; stale ---
# --- host-side copies (if any exist) must never be copied in instead ---
**/node_modules
**/build
**/dist
**/.react-router
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- unrelated workspace content: not read by apps/dash/Dockerfile at all ---
/assets
/data
/pipeline
/.github
/.superpowers
/apps/web/public
/apps/web/src
